		(uuid "02974a0c-3b8e-57db-bf0f-e29d37d9e813")
	)
	(text
		"J_SOIL2 pin1 and pin2 are the probe, pin3 GND. AC excitation: the probe is driven with alternating polarity from two GPIOs through R_S2 and R_D2 (10 k each), so it never sees DC. Firmware: in each phase both nodes are sampled (SOIL2_ADC_A and SOIL2_ADC_B) with one pin driven high and the other low; phase 2 reverses the drive. With Vd = V(A) - V(B) in a phase, I = 3.3 V / (20 k + Rprobe) and Vd = 3.3 V x Rprobe / (20 k + Rprobe), so Rprobe = 20 k x Vd / (3.3 V - Vd), which cancels the drive level and the 10 k tolerances; Vd is 0.157 V at 1 k and 3.0 V at 200 k. Between measurements both drive pins are set low or to Hi-Z, so the probe sees no DC.  R_F2 and R_F2B 1 k with C_F2 and C_F2B 10 nF filter the ADC inputs. D_ESD_S2 (PRTR5V0U2X) protects the connector pins."
		(at 16.74 113.11 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "6cc6a383-4605-565a-8dfd-a45dfc218b14")
	)
